      "question": {
        "math_academy_id": "q-116296",
        "knowledge_point_id": "bec73486-156f-5124-97b4-58f65ea8430d",
        "knowledge_point": "Using the Trapezoidal Rule With Irregular Step Size",
        "problem": "Using the trapezoidal rule with the partition\n\n$$\n[1,5]=[1,2]\\cup [2,5],\n$$\n\napproximate the area under the curve of the continuous function $y=f(x)$ whose data is given in the table below.\n\n| $x$ | $1$ | $2$ | $5$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $f(x)$ | $1$ | $3$ | $7$ |",
        "worked_solution": "Let's plot what this function might look like, using the values given in the table.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14055663/assets/8fe84e0056eaa8320b4824740a259226b1a18ff1b64ba648d8740d6cac8703fc.png)\n\nWe've drawn some trapezoids to help calculate our trapezoidal rule sum. By calculating the area of each trapezoid, we obtain the following approximation for our area $A:$\n\n$$\nA≈\\overset{1\\text{st trapezoid}}{\\overset{⏞}{[\\,\\frac{\\overset{\\text{bases}}{\\overset{⏞}{f(1)+f(2)}}}{2}\\,\\cdot \\,{{Δ{x}_{1}}_{⏟}}_{\\text{height}}\\,]}}+\\overset{2\\text{nd trapezoid}}{\\overset{⏞}{[\\,\\frac{\\overset{\\text{bases}}{\\overset{⏞}{f(2)+f(5)}}}{2}\\,\\cdot \\,{{Δ{x}_{2}}_{⏟}}_{\\text{height}}\\,]}}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the appropriate numbers into the above expression gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & ≈\\frac{1+3}{2}\\cdot (2-1)+\\frac{3+7}{2}\\cdot (5-2) \\\\  & =2\\cdot 1+5\\cdot 3 \\\\  & =2+15 \\\\  & =17.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
