    {
      "directory": "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14055789",
      "id": "q-8873",
      "status": "supported",
      "reason": null,
      "question": {
        "math_academy_id": "q-8873",
        "knowledge_point_id": "bf1a53c0-e652-5732-9d5a-5aad004c2676",
        "knowledge_point": "Solving Trigonometric Equations Using the Sin-Cos-Tan Identity Under a Modified Domain",
        "problem": "Given that ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ are the solutions to the equation $8\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+4\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=0$ for $-\\pi <x\\le \\pi ,$ what is the value of ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2},$ rounded to $2$ decimal places?",
        "worked_solution": "We divide both sides of the equation by $\\operatorname{cos}⁡x$ and use the identity $\\operatorname{tan}⁡x=\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}.$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}8\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+4\\operatorname{cos}⁡x & =0 \\\\ \\frac{8\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}+\\frac{4\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x} & =0 \\\\ \\frac{8\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}+\\frac{4\\cancel{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}}{\\cancel{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}} & =0 \\\\ 8\\cdot \\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}+4 & =0 \\\\ 8\\operatorname{tan}⁡x+4 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we rearrange the equation and isolate $\\operatorname{tan}⁡x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}8\\operatorname{tan}⁡x+4 & =0 \\\\ 8\\operatorname{tan}⁡x & =-4 \\\\ \\operatorname{tan}⁡x & =-\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we find the principal value:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(-\\frac{1}{2})=-0.463\\,647…≈-0.463\\,65\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to $5$ decimal places.\n\nSince $-0.463\\,65$ lies inside the given domain, our first solution is ${x}_{1}=-0.463\\,65.$\n\nTo find the other solution, we add $\\pi $ to the principal value. Hence,\n\n$$\n{x}_{2}=-0.463\\,65…+\\pi ≈2.677\\,95\n$$\n\nrounded to $5$ decimal places.\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}≈-0.463\\,65\\cdot 2.677\\,95≈-1.24\n$$\n\nrounded to two decimal places.",
        "answer_fields": [
          {
            "key": "selection",
            "type": "radio",
            "choices_complete": true,
            "choices": [
              {
                "type": "math",
                "value": "2.74",
